# Attach contract — new ISA is not a copy of emit/c

File: oodac/docs/x86-codegen-style.oot

Product oodac emits C99 and gcc. That C path is the reference, not a forever ban on other ISAs.

The C reference gate is: four product mains `check`, product `build` of ooda/lsp/mcp, and the unique_fns host rebuild of `oodac/main.oo` (`OK_PURE_MULTI`, `PURE_SKIP_CHECK` unset). Concat of `oodac/main.oo` as the only compiler ELF is a fail.

A later `--backend` (llvm or wasm) is a new directory `emit/<name>/` that consumes the same typed artifact C uses. Shared type names (`OoResI`, list kinds, cap tokens) live in `types/`. If C and the new backend disagree, the new backend is wrong until a hostile probe that C already passes says otherwise.

Do not restore `x86_emit_*.oo` or `cli_emit_llvm.oo` as product. Do not put GNU statement-expr or `__typeof__` in C lowering.

Status: C is the reference. A second consumer of the typed artifact may attach.
